 ("p", "The **atmosphere** is the blanket of air held around the Earth by **gravity** (the force of attraction the Earth exerts on objects on or near its surface). It is a mixture of gases vital for life. It:"),
 ("ul", ["shields us from harmful radiation of the Sun, including ultraviolet rays;", "regulates the Earth's temperature by trapping some of the Sun's energy and preventing it from escaping to space;", "is a key part of weather and climate, influencing temperature, humidity and air pressure."]),
 ("h2", "Composition and Structure of the Atmosphere"),
