 ("note", "DEFINITION", "**Aurora:** colourful light display near the poles. Charged particles of the **solar wind** are guided to the magnetic poles and make atmospheric gases glow. Called **Aurora Borealis** in the Northern Hemisphere and **Aurora Australis** in the Southern. 'Aurora' is Latin for dawn, after the Roman goddess of dawn."),
