 ("note", "IMPORTANT", "**Importance of monsoon:** most Indian agriculture depends on it; it governs food production and water in rivers, reservoirs and wells; it affects transport, festivals and rural jobs. Excess rain causes floods; weak monsoon causes drought. Hence it shapes the economy and livelihoods and gives the country climatic unity."),
 ("h3", "Knowledge traditions and missions"),
 ("ul", ["**Kṛiṣhiparāśhara** predicted rainfall from positions of the Moon and Sun; **Varāhamihira's Bṛihatsaṁhitā** used **nakṣhatras** (lunar mansions: sky divided into 27 parts along the Moon's path; the Moon takes about 27 days to circle and moves through about one nakṣhatra a day). Many Indian farming practices still follow these methods.", "**Kālidāsa's Meghadūtam** (about 5th century CE) mentions the onset date of the monsoon over central India and traces the path of monsoon clouds.", "**National Monsoon Mission (NMM)**, Ministry of Earth Sciences, builds weather and climate prediction models. **Mission Mausam** aims to make India 'Weather Ready' and 'Climate Smart' with better observation, modelling and forecasting for agriculture, disaster management and rural development."]),
 ("note", "NOTE", "Monsoon advances: normal onset begins on about 22 May in the far south and reaches north-west India by about 8 July; retreat begins about 17 September from the north-west and ends about 15 October in the south."),
 ("h2", "Climate Change"),
 ("p", "**Climate change** is the long-term change in weather patterns (temperature, rainfall, wind) caused mainly by human activities: burning fossil fuels, deforestation and industrial pollution. These raise **greenhouse gases** (carbon dioxide, methane, nitrous oxide, water vapour), which trap heat and raise global temperatures."),
 ("table", ["Effects", "Details"], [["Environmental", "More floods and droughts, melting glaciers, rising sea level, loss of biodiversity"], ["Human", "Health, agriculture and livelihoods; affects all sections including women and children"]]),
 ("note", "DEFINITION", "**Carbon footprint:** total greenhouse gases released into the atmosphere by human activities such as energy use, transport and production of goods and services."),
 ("p", "**Ways to reduce it:** save energy and switch off appliances, use renewable energy, walk/cycle/use public transport or carpool, avoid single-use plastics and reuse/recycle, save water, protect forests and plant trees, adopt sustainable lifestyles. Self-check categories: transport, electricity, water, waste and plastics (low impact = 1 point to very high = 4 points); then pledge two changes."),
 ("h2", "Case Study: Punjab Floods, 2025"),
 ("p", "Heavy monsoon rains and swelling of the rivers **Satluj, Beas and Ravi** (and the Ghaggar) flooded large parts of Punjab, damaging villages, fields, houses, roads and bridges."),
 ("table", ["Natural causes", "Human-made causes"], [
  ["Very heavy monsoon rain, intensified by **western disturbances**; heavy rain also in Himachal Pradesh and Jammu & Kashmir; rivers already flowing high", "Weak, old embankments (**dhūsī bāndh**); houses and farms built too close to rivers; silt in rivers and dams reducing capacity; late or unclear flood warnings"]]),
 ("ul", ["**Effects:** deaths; thousands moved to relief camps; paddy and other crops damaged; poultry and dairy losses (cows, buffaloes, chickens); roads, bridges, border fences and public buildings damaged; standing water caused waterborne disease and sanitation problems.", "**Lessons:** better flood management, embankment repair, desilting, regulated building near rivers, timely warnings and disaster preparedness (NDMA guidelines)."]),
